window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>In the tenth volume of the Xane series, author Mark White delves into the complex emotion of pride. Xane finds herself at the center of a storm when Zoe, a bandmate, reveals her deep-seated pride, causing tension and division within the band. As Zoe's arrogance threatens to tear the group apart, Xane must navigate the delicate balance between healthy pride and destructive hubris.</p> <p>Guided by the Analyst, Xane learns that pride can be both empowering and isolating. Through introspective conversations and challenging interactions with her bandmates, Xane discovers the importance of humility and teamwork. As the band prepares for a high-stakes music video shoot, they face technical difficulties and interpersonal conflicts that test their resilience and unity.</p> <p><i>Pride</i> is a powerful exploration of emotional intelligence, highlighting the complexities of pride and the importance of humility in overcoming negative emotions. Join Xane and her bandmates as they learn to navigate pride, set emotional boundaries, and find strength in their journey. This volume is a must-listen for fans of the series and anyone interested in the intricate dance of emotions.</p>"; 
